WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.000
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.501
Thank you for being here. Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:10.234
Guys, here's some much-needed good news.

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:12.067
Beyoncé just announced that next month

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:15.434
she's releasing a new album called "Renaissance."

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:17.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:21.934
Then everyone else releasing an album was like,

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.667
"Okay, August it is. Uh..."

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:30.067
This will be Beyoncé's first album since 2016.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.467
Come on. That's too long. That's too long.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:33.634
In that same time,

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:35.267
Taylor Swift's released 42 albums.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:37.367
I mean, come on.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:39.167
Of course, fans are pumped for the album.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:41.133
Seriously, the only thing going more platinum

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.868
is Ryan Gosling as Ken. You know?

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.300
-Hey.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:48.734
-Yeah. That's right.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.834
This is big news for the music business

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:53.767
and even bigger news for the wind-machine industry.

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:55.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:57.300
Guys, get this.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.067
Today, for the first time, Elon Musk met virtually

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:03.200
with Twitter employees at a company-wide meeting.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.367
[ Audience oohs ] Ooh.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.501
Employees called it good practice

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:12.334
for that awkward phone call with Dad on Father's Day.

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:15.234
Yeah, picture the awkwardness of a Zoom happy hour

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.801
times 44 billion. You know what I'm saying?

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.267
Some more business news --

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:21.868
I heard that Facebook is planning a major redesign

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:24.701
on its main feed to help it compete with TikTok.

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:27.167
[ Audience oohs ] When people accused them

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.067
of copying TikTok, Facebook said,

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:31.367
"We're not copying TikTok. We're duetting with TikTok."

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:33.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.868
Hey, did you guys see this?

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:37.000
A British Airways flight got a little hectic

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.267
when water started flooding from the ceiling

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:42.300
while the plane was in air.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.834
Look at this. This is scary.

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:45.400
-Ohh.

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.133
-Yeah. At that point, the pilot was like,

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:51.267
"Uh, tonight's in-flight entertainment

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:54.601
is anyone who wants to re-enact that scene from 'The Notebook.'

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:58.400
You can just...go for it."

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.234
But everyone just made the best of it.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:01.934
They just turned the inflatable chute

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:03.567
into a Slip 'N Slide.

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:04.901
It was fun. It was fun.

00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:06.634
I love that.

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:08.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:12.067
I did a stand-up.

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.534
I was doing a stand-up Slip 'N Slide.

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:14.834
-Yeah, I saw that. It was like --

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.634
More like a Slip 'N -- like Surf 'N Slide.

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.234
-Yeah, well, I mean, that's what you do

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:19.734
at the advanced level.

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.300
'Cause obviously you do the belly flop and go --

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.467
slide right down, but then you get muddy and all that stuff,

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:24.934
and then by the end of the afternoon,

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:27.200
you get bored and you go, "Let me try this."

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.667
-So you do it up. You do it standing up.

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:29.934
Yeah.

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:32.801
♪♪

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:34.934
-Look out, look out, look out!

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.701
Wipeout!

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:38.400
[ Steve imitating "Wipeout" giggle ]

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.334
-What? Wha--

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:42.567
-That was the "Wipeout"...

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:43.801
-Of course. -Yeah.

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:47.334
-Uh, hey, guys, I saw that Disney is offering

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:49.200
a new high-end travel package

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.133
called Disney Parks Around the World,

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:52.868
where you travel on a private jet

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:55.968
to all their parks for $110,000.

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:58.534
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:01.501
But they're not the only theme park

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:03.033
offering a deluxe package, though.

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:04.234
No. Watch this.

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:06.701
-Can't afford Disney's Around the World tickets?

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:09.968
Then book your spot on the Busch Gardens VIP Tour.

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:11.434
[ Coughing ]

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:14.734
For just $65.99, you'll get to climb aboard

00:03:14.734 --> 00:03:16.734
this magical chariot... [ Horn honking ]

00:03:16.734 --> 00:03:19.167
...while enjoying the finest of beverages...

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:22.200
and sampling the freshest foods as you're chauffeured

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.934
between the London and Paris of America,

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:26.300
Virginia and Tampa.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.968
[ Clearing throat ]

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.834
When you see what looks like an abandoned

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:32.667
haunted amusement park, you've arrived.

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:34.367
The Busch Gardens VIP Tour.

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:36.701
Make sure you got your tetanus shot!

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:38.467
-Wow. That was...

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:40.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:47.200
-Hey, guys, with summer movie season here,

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.367
there's tons of great stuff in theaters right now,

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:50.467
so I wanted to run down

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.100
everything worth seeing in a new segment.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.667
It's time for "The Tonight Show Hollywood Pop Corner."

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.000
Here we go.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.067
-♪ Hollywood Pop Corner ♪

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:03.300
♪ The Hollywood Pop Corner ♪

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.501
♪ Hollywood Pop Corner ♪

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:08.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.934
-You're in "Hollywood Pop Corner."

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:12.467
Let's roll picture.

00:04:12.467 --> 00:04:13.834
"Lightyear."

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:15.934
You won't need a light beer to enjoy "Lightyear."

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:18.901
In fact, the only buzz I got was from actor Chris Evans,

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:21.033
who'll have audiences in bliss heavens.

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:23.133
Should you see it? I Holly would.

