00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:01.434
Remember to silence your cellphones.

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:03.534
I'll see you at the claw machine in the lobby!

00:06:03.534 --> 00:06:07.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:10.200
-♪ Hollywood Pop Corner ♪

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:13.400
♪ The Hollywood Pop Corner ♪

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.834
♪ Hollywood Pop Corner ♪

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:19.801
-Wow.

00:06:19.801 --> 00:06:21.567
How much popcorn --

00:06:21.567 --> 00:06:24.334
I ate one piece of popcorn.

00:06:24.334 --> 00:06:25.801
-And it went right down your throat.

00:06:25.801 --> 00:06:27.934
-I coughed, like, 30 pieces up.

00:06:27.934 --> 00:06:30.067
I don't know what I did. I don't know how I did that.

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:31.567
-I didn't know that was you.

00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:33.601
-Oh, you thought it was a different --

00:06:33.601 --> 00:06:35.267
-Yeah. -Thank you. Amazing.

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:36.667
No, I was just acting.

00:06:36.667 --> 00:06:39.167
That was me in a wig acting as a film critic.

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:41.300
-Oh, my God! I was not aware of that!

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.367
-Well, there you go. -My gosh! Bravo!

00:06:43.367 --> 00:06:44.834
-Thank you very much.

00:06:44.834 --> 00:06:47.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:47.334 --> 00:06:48.701
Guys, listen to this.

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:51.067
Researchers say that an anti-hunger pill

00:06:51.067 --> 00:06:54.567
is on the horizon that could replace the need for exercise.

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:56.067
[ Audience oohs ]

00:06:56.067 --> 00:06:58.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:58.534 --> 00:07:00.234
When they heard, Peloton was like,

00:07:00.234 --> 00:07:02.667
"Okay, things can get worse. Alright."

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:04.534
Hey, I read about a bus driver

00:07:04.534 --> 00:07:06.901
who was found passed out on the side of the highway,

00:07:06.901 --> 00:07:08.167
and he said that he didn't know

00:07:08.167 --> 00:07:10.968
that the gummies he was eating had THC in them.

00:07:10.968 --> 00:07:13.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:13.534 --> 00:07:17.701
Even more upsetting, he's the most sober driver in the fleet.

00:07:17.701 --> 00:07:19.901
And finally, guys, there's so many cool things to do

00:07:19.901 --> 00:07:21.667
here in New York, and there's a brand-new

00:07:21.667 --> 00:07:23.467
roller-skating attraction opening tonight

00:07:23.467 --> 00:07:25.567
called the DiscOasis Central Park.

00:07:25.567 --> 00:07:28.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:28.367 --> 00:07:30.601
I had to check it out, so I called my pal Keke Palmer.

00:07:30.601 --> 00:07:32.467
I said, "You wanna go skating in the park?"

00:07:32.467 --> 00:07:34.834
She said, "Of course." So check this out.

00:07:34.834 --> 00:07:38.000
[ Cheers and applause ] ♪♪

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.634
Hi, guys. Jimmy Fallon here.

00:07:39.634 --> 00:07:42.534
I'm at the DiscOasis Central Park in New York City.

00:07:42.534 --> 00:07:43.601
It is a roller rink.

00:07:43.601 --> 00:07:45.601
It is a disco-immersive experience.

00:07:45.601 --> 00:07:46.701
It is a party.

00:07:46.701 --> 00:07:47.868
Right now, I'm going to put my

00:07:47.868 --> 00:07:49.534
roller-skating skills to the test.

00:07:49.534 --> 00:07:51.467
I'm going to get my skates on, and let's do this.

00:07:51.467 --> 00:07:54.334
[ The Trammps' "Disco Inferno" plays ]

00:07:59.234 --> 00:08:01.200
-♪ Burn, baby, burn ♪

00:08:02.868 --> 00:08:04.200
♪ Burn, baby, burn ♪

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.300
-♪ Hey! ♪

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.300
[ Slow disco music playing ]

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.534
[ Music stops ]

00:08:11.534 --> 00:08:13.334
[ Record scratches ]

00:08:13.334 --> 00:08:14.767
-We're not doing the costumes?

00:08:14.767 --> 00:08:16.567
-Unh-unh.

00:08:16.567 --> 00:08:17.634
-Okay.

00:08:17.634 --> 00:08:20.467
♪♪

00:08:20.467 --> 00:08:22.701
-We're here with Khalil "Gifted" Johnson.

00:08:22.701 --> 00:08:23.968
Thanks for having us.

00:08:23.968 --> 00:08:26.634
You look great. Clearly, I don't.

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:29.067
What would you tell someone who's just learning

00:08:29.067 --> 00:08:30.334
to roller-skate -- any advice?

00:08:30.334 --> 00:08:32.167
-Always have a bend in your knees.

00:08:32.167 --> 00:08:33.467
-Right? -A.k.a. balance.

00:08:33.467 --> 00:08:35.934
-I feel like I'm at a good balance right now.

00:08:35.934 --> 00:08:37.167
I feel like I can do this.

00:08:37.167 --> 00:08:38.968
You're one of the expert roller skaters here,

00:08:38.968 --> 00:08:41.033
and you're going to teach Keke and I a few moves

00:08:41.033 --> 00:08:42.868
so that we'll be able to join your team

00:08:42.868 --> 00:08:44.033
for a big performance later, right?

00:08:44.033 --> 00:08:45.300
-Yes, sir. -Okay.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:47.667
-So, it's a simple move, right? Shoot the duck.

00:08:47.667 --> 00:08:49.300
-"Shoot the duck." That sounds like something cool.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.567
-I'm gonna pick up that right leg.

00:08:50.567 --> 00:08:51.601
-Alright. -Right?

00:08:51.601 --> 00:08:53.834
And then drop down.

00:08:53.834 --> 00:08:54.868
[ Laughs ]

00:08:54.868 --> 00:08:56.200
-Squat down. -Uh-huh.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:58.501
-We got this! -Yeah, he did! Yeah, he did!

00:08:58.501 --> 00:09:00.100
-Whoo! -Yes. Yes.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:01.334
-Ow! Ow!

00:09:01.334 --> 00:09:03.000
What's the other move?

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.400
-Alright, now, now.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:06.767
-So, your first step is going to be here.

00:09:06.767 --> 00:09:08.000
-So we go...this?

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.400
-Yeah, yeah.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.567
-This. -Yeah.

00:09:10.634 --> 00:09:11.901
-This. -Yeah.

00:09:11.901 --> 00:09:15.033
-Why do I look like this and you look like that?

00:09:15.033 --> 00:09:16.067
-Let's crossover.

00:09:16.067 --> 00:09:17.167
-Crossover? -Crossover.

00:09:17.167 --> 00:09:18.434
Oh, that means I'm gonna die.

00:09:18.434 --> 00:09:19.834
That's what that -- You can't say "crossover."

00:09:19.834 --> 00:09:21.868
-Step.

00:09:21.868 --> 00:09:23.567
Now we're going to put all your weight on the right side.

00:09:23.567 --> 00:09:24.667
-This looks so -- I just saw --

00:09:24.667 --> 00:09:27.200
I saw my shadow, and it's so embarrassing.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:28.534
My shadow is embarrassing.

00:09:28.534 --> 00:09:30.033
-Crossover. -1, 2.

00:09:30.033 --> 00:09:31.634
-Yes, sir. -Crossover.

00:09:31.634 --> 00:09:33.934
-Go back the other way. -1, 2.

00:09:33.934 --> 00:09:35.000
1, 2.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.467
-You hit that!

00:09:36.467 --> 00:09:37.601
-Really? That was...

00:09:37.601 --> 00:09:38.667
-Let's get it.

00:09:38.667 --> 00:09:39.667
-Let's do it! -Let's do it.

00:09:39.667 --> 00:09:40.767
-Let's do it. ♪♪

00:09:40.767 --> 00:09:43.400
-Oh, now that's what I'm talking about.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:46.868
♪♪

00:09:46.868 --> 00:09:49.367
-♪ These are the good times ♪

00:09:49.367 --> 00:09:50.934
-Whoo! Get it.

00:09:50.934 --> 00:09:53.400
-♪ Leave your cares behind ♪

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.234
That's all -- Yeah, that's all I can really do.

00:09:55.234 --> 00:09:56.667
So, what do you think? Are we ready to perform?

00:09:56.667 --> 00:09:57.901
-I think you guys got it.

00:09:57.901 --> 00:09:59.267
-Let's do this. -Let's do it, man.

00:09:59.267 --> 00:10:00.834
♪♪

00:10:00.834 --> 00:10:02.067
-Hold on. -I can't. I can't.

00:10:02.067 --> 00:10:03.267
-I got you. I'll catch you.

00:10:03.267 --> 00:10:04.667
-Pull me back. -He good, he good.

00:10:04.667 --> 00:10:09.701
-And now the DiscOasis Dancers featuring Keke and Jimmy.

00:10:09.701 --> 00:10:15.200
♪♪

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:17.200
[ Rhythmic clapping ]

00:10:21.634 --> 00:10:23.467
[ Cheers and applause ] -We did it, guys!

00:10:23.467 --> 00:10:25.601
-Yes! [ All cheering ]

00:10:25.601 --> 00:10:27.834
We killed it! -You did it!

00:10:27.834 --> 00:10:29.968
-Yes! Keke, take me home.

00:10:29.968 --> 00:10:31.267
-Okay. Let's go.

00:10:31.267 --> 00:10:35.167
[ The Trammps' "Disco Inferno" plays ]

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:37.367
♪ Burn, baby, burn ♪

00:10:37.367 --> 00:10:39.334
-♪ Disco inferno ♪

00:10:39.334 --> 00:10:41.434
-Oh, my thanks to Keke Palmer.

00:10:41.434 --> 00:10:43.100
Go see her new movie, "Lightyear,"

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.567
in theaters this Friday.

00:10:44.567 --> 00:10:45.934
I love Keke Palmer.

00:10:45.934 --> 00:10:48.133
[ Cheers and applause ] She's the one.

00:10:48.133 --> 00:10:50.834
And thank you to everyone at DiscOasis Central Park.

00:10:50.834 --> 00:10:52.200
If you're in New York, go check it out.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.167
It's now through the end of the summer.

00:10:54.167 --> 00:10:55.467
We have a great show.

